# Catalog and evidence

- Git bytes are repository truth for tracked files; Catalog is discovery metadata.
- Do not copy the seven ChatGPT Project Sources into Git as a second permanent-memory owner.
- Do not invent past `first_reliable_available_at` availability.
- Exact imported pre-Git bytes stay under `docs/evidence/pre_git/`.
- Do not manually edit generated Catalog navigation or `docs/PROJECT_MAP.md` unless the atom explicitly authorizes that write set.
- Machine-specific absolute paths must not enter Catalog metadata.
- See `AGENTS.md` and existing Catalog/ADR docs for integrity rules.
